---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { arc, partnerBoard } from '../../data/partners/index';

// The board section is data-driven: partnerBoard returns the Arc board only once
// results/arc.json exists and carries rows. Until then the page states that
// measurement is pending and shows no number it cannot source.
const board = partnerBoard(arc);
const pts = (v: number) => v.toFixed(1);
const ladder = arc.ladder ?? [];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Arc"
  description="Arc is Circle's USDC-native L1 with a confidential compute sector. The arc benchmark vertical measures whether coding agents can build on it, from a single contract up to a running system with a keeper, an indexer, and a CLI, all graded by execution."
  bodyClass="page-editorial"
>
  <section class="pt-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <a class="pt-back" href="/partners">&larr; Partners</a>
      <div class="pt-role mono">{arc.role}</div>
      <h1>{arc.name}</h1>
      <p class="pt-lede">
        Arc is Circle's USDC-native L1: USDC is the gas token, and the Arc Privacy Sector runs a
        private EVM inside hardware enclaves alongside the public chain, with encrypted state and
        shield and unshield bridging between the two.
        The <span class="mono">arc</span> benchmark vertical asks a narrower question about it.
        Can a coding agent actually build on this chain, and at what scope does it stop?
      </p>
      <div class="pt-facts mono">
        <span><strong>{arc.taskCount}</strong> execution-graded tasks</span>
        <span><strong>{arc.difficultyMix?.hard}</strong> hard, <strong>{arc.difficultyMix?.extreme}</strong> extreme</span>
        <span>testnet chain id <strong>5042002</strong></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pt-body">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="pt-block">
        <h2>What the vertical measures</h2>
        <p class="pt-p">
          Most agent benchmarks ask for one artifact and check whether it compiles.
          That question stopped separating models: a strong open-weight model one-shots a lending
          vault graded by fuzzing and stateful invariants.
          So the <span class="mono">arc</span> vertical is built as a ladder instead of a pile.
          Tasks escalate by the number of components a solution needs and by the seams between them,
          and every task sits in one vertical so a run reports where a model stops rather than which
          bucket it happened to draw from.
        </p>
        <p class="pt-p">
          A single contract can be subtly wrong in one place. A system can be subtly wrong in the
          joints: a keeper that watches but never acts, an indexer that double counts an event, a CLI
          that disagrees with the chain. Those are the failures the upper rungs are built to catch.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-block">
        <h2>The ladder</h2>
        <div class="pt-rungs">
          {ladder.map((r) => (
            <div class="pt-rung">
              <div class="pt-rung-head">
                <span class="pt-rung-level mono">{r.level}</span>
                <h3>{r.name}</h3>
                <span class="pt-rung-count mono">{r.tasks} task{r.tasks === 1 ? '' : 's'}</span>
              </div>
              <div class="pt-rung-grid">
                <div class="pt-rung-cell">
                  <h4>What the agent builds</h4>
                  <p>{r.shape}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pt-rung-cell">
                  <h4>How it is graded</h4>
                  <p>{r.grader}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="pt-example">
                <div class="pt-example-label mono">Example task &middot; <span>{r.example.id}</span></div>
                <p>{r.example.summary}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="pt-note">
          Rung counts are the authored tasks in
          <span class="mono">{arc.verticalSource}</span>, counted from the vertical itself.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-block">
        <h2>How a task is graded</h2>
        <p class="pt-p">
          Every task is graded by running code, never by asking a model whether the work looks right.
          The grader for a task is a hidden program, and the exit code it returns is the score.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-method-grid">
          <div class="pt-m">
            <h3>The tests are not in the workspace</h3>
            <p>
              The hidden test suite is decoded into a temporary directory outside the directory the
              agent works in, and reads the agent's work only through a path handed to it. An agent
              cannot read the tests, edit them, or write a solution that targets them.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pt-m">
            <h3>Adversarial, not confirmatory</h3>
            <p>
              Contract tasks are graded by fuzzing, stateful invariants, and attack contracts that try
              to break the agent's contract, rather than by a happy-path check that a correct-looking
              implementation passes by accident.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pt-m">
            <h3>Whole systems run for real</h3>
            <p>
              At the system rung the grader boots a chain, deploys the agent's contracts, starts the
              agent's keeper, indexer, and CLI as real processes, drives a scenario, and asserts
              on-chain state, HTTP responses, and CLI output against each other.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="pt-m">
            <h3>Fail closed</h3>
            <p>
              The grader checks that the required files exist before it decodes anything. A missing
              deliverable exits before grading starts, so an empty or partial submission can never be
              scored against a grader that quietly does nothing.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-block">
        <h2>Calibration receipts</h2>
        <p class="pt-p">
          A task is admitted to the vertical only after it is run three ways, and the receipt is kept
          with the task. A reference implementation has to pass. A plausible but wrong implementation
          has to fail, and it has to fail on the specific rule the task exists to teach rather than on
          something incidental. An empty submission has to fail closed. If a wrong solution passes, the
          task is not measuring anything and does not ship.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-receipts-scroll">
          <table class="pt-receipts">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Task</th>
                <th>Reference</th>
                <th>Plausible but wrong</th>
                <th>Empty</th>
                <th>The trap it catches</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td class="pt-r-id mono">arc-agent-job-escrow</td>
                <td class="pt-r-pass mono">passes 7 of 7</td>
                <td class="pt-r-fail mono">fails 4 of 7</td>
                <td class="pt-r-fail mono">fails closed</td>
                <td>Access control, state machine order, and paying out exactly once</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="pt-r-id mono">aps-trust-domain-engine</td>
                <td class="pt-r-pass mono">passes 11 of 11</td>
                <td class="pt-r-fail mono">fails 9</td>
                <td class="pt-r-fail mono">fails closed</td>
                <td>Deny by default, and trust that flows one way and stays revocable</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="pt-r-id mono">aps-light-client-commit</td>
                <td class="pt-r-pass mono">passes 11 of 11</td>
                <td class="pt-r-fail mono">fails 6</td>
                <td class="pt-r-fail mono">fails closed</td>
                <td>A strict two thirds threshold, and verifying before mutating state</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="pt-r-id mono">lending market with keeper</td>
                <td class="pt-r-pass mono">system works</td>
                <td class="pt-r-fail mono">keeper never acts</td>
                <td class="pt-r-fail mono">fails closed</td>
                <td>A component that looks finished but never moves the chain</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="pt-note">
          Receipts are recorded in the vertical source and in
          <span class="mono">docs/research/arc-canteen/harness-proof/</span>, against the same grader
          command a scored run uses.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-block" id="board">
        <h2>The board</h2>
        {board ? (
          <div>
            <p class="pt-p">
              {board.rows.length} agent{board.rows.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} have been scored on the
              {' '}{board.taskCount ?? arc.taskCount}-task suite.
            </p>
            <div class="pt-roster-scroll">
              <table class="pt-roster">
                <thead>
                  <tr><th>Agent</th><th>Harness</th><th>Pass rate</th><th>Passed / graded</th><th>Run date</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {[...board.rows].sort((a, b) => (b.passRate ?? b.score) - (a.passRate ?? a.score)).map((row) => (
                    <tr>
                      <td class="pt-r-model">{row.model}</td>
                      <td>{row.harness ?? 'direct'}</td>
                      <td class="pt-r-score mono">{pts((row.passRate ?? row.score) * 100)}</td>
                      <td class="mono">{Math.round((row.passRate ?? row.score) * row.n)} / {row.n}</td>
                      <td class="mono">{row.date}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <a class="pt-board-link" href={`/benchmarks/${board.id}`}>Full board with the per-task breakdown &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        ) : (
          <div class="pt-pending">
            <div class="pt-pending-badge mono">measurement pending</div>
            <p>
              The {arc.taskCount} tasks are authored and calibrated, and no model roster has been run
              against them yet, so there is no score on this page.
              When the sweep completes, the ranked results appear here and on a full board with the
              per-task breakdown. Until then Arc carries no number, on this page or anywhere else on
              this site.
            </p>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pt-cta">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Run the suite against your chain</h2>
      <p>
        We author the tasks, calibrate every one three ways, run the roster, and publish the results
        with their coverage attached. If you want a suite built for your protocol, or run against a
        release before it ships, write to us.
      </p>
      <div class="pt-cta-row">
        <a class="pt-btn" href="mailto:hello@tangle.tools?subject=Arc%20benchmark">hello@tangle.tools</a>
        <a class="pt-btn ghost" href="/partners/canteen">How the tasks were grounded &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .shell { width: min(72rem, 92vw); margin: 0 auto; }
  .mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-feature-settings: 'tnum'; }

  .pt-hero { background: var(--paper-1); padding: 2.5rem 0 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); }
  .pt-back { color: #4F46E5; font-size: 0.9rem; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; }
  .pt-back:hover { color: #4338CA; }
  .pt-role { margin-top: 1.4rem; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .pt-hero h1 { margin: 0.4rem 0 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.035em; color: var(--ink); font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); }
  .pt-lede { margin: 1.1rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.4vw, 1.28rem); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 50rem; }
  .pt-facts { display: flex; gap: 1.4rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.6rem; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .pt-facts strong { color: #4F46E5; }

  .pt-body { background: var(--paper-0); padding: 3rem 0 2rem; }
  .pt-block { margin-bottom: 3.2rem; scroll-margin-top: 2rem; }
  .pt-block h2, .pt-cta h2 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.7rem; }
  .pt-p { margin: 1rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 52rem; }
  .pt-note { margin: 0.9rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 52rem; }
  .pt-note .mono { color: var(--ink-secondary); }

  /* ladder: one card per rung, each carrying its shape, grader, and a real task */
  .pt-rungs { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .pt-rung { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); border-radius: 15px; padding: 1.3rem 1.4rem; box-shadow: 0 8px 26px rgba(25,28,60,0.05); }
  .pt-rung-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.7rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .pt-rung-level { color: #fff; background: #4F46E5; font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 6px; letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
  .pt-rung-head h3 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .pt-rung-count { margin-left: auto; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .pt-rung-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(17rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .pt-rung-cell h4 { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .pt-rung-cell p { margin: 0.4rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .pt-example { margin-top: 1.1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); padding-top: 0.9rem; }
  .pt-example-label { color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .pt-example-label span { color: #4F46E5; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; }
  .pt-example p { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; }

  .pt-method-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .pt-m { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem; box-shadow: 0 8px 26px rgba(25,28,60,0.05); }
  .pt-m h3 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .pt-m p { margin: 0.55rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; }

  .pt-receipts-scroll, .pt-roster-scroll { margin-top: 1.5rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(25,28,60,0.06); }
  .pt-receipts, .pt-roster { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 44rem; }
  .pt-receipts thead th, .pt-roster thead th { text-align: left; padding: 0.8rem 1rem; color: var(--ink-muted); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); white-space: nowrap; }
  .pt-receipts tbody td, .pt-roster tbody td { padding: 0.7rem 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); color: var(--ink-secondary); vertical-align: top; }
  .pt-receipts tbody tr:first-child td, .pt-roster tbody tr:first-child td { border-top: none; }
  .pt-r-id { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pt-r-pass { color: #047857; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pt-r-fail { color: #9A3412; font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pt-r-model { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .pt-r-score { color: #4F46E5; font-weight: 700; }
  .pt-board-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1.1rem; color: #4F46E5; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .pt-board-link:hover { color: #4338CA; }

  /* honest degradation: no chart, no zeros, no placeholder rows */
  .pt-pending { margin-top: 1.5rem; border: 1px dashed var(--hairline-light); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--paper-1); padding: 2rem 1.6rem; }
  .pt-pending-badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--ink-muted); background: var(--paper-2); padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem; border-radius: 999px; }
  .pt-pending p { margin: 1rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 48rem; }

  .pt-cta { background: var(--paper-1); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-light); padding: 3.5rem 0 4.5rem; }
  .pt-cta p { margin: 1rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 48rem; }
  .pt-cta-row { display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .pt-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; padding: 0.55rem 1.05rem; border-radius: 9px; background: #4F46E5; color: #fff; transition: background 0.15s; }
  .pt-btn:hover { background: #4338CA; }
  .pt-btn.ghost { background: transparent; color: #4F46E5; border: 1px solid rgba(79,70,229,0.35); }
  .pt-btn.ghost:hover { background: rgba(79,70,229,0.06); }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .pt-block h2, .pt-cta h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; }
    .pt-rung-count { margin-left: 0; }
  }
</style>
